[Music]  i use not only design but biology  to create new materials which actually  are fully sustainable and biodegradable  my first material that i focused on  developing  was sweat crystallization this was a  method that i worked alongside with  imperial college of  collecting people's sweat and extracting  out basically the sodiums the lactic  acids  and the estrogen to make these  bio crystals which are then embellished  onto these fashioned  materials i also developed bio-based  plastics unlike most bio  plastics which are available in market  is made a hundred percent  from natural ingredients so mine is a  base  of different things like seaweed flowers  and natural earth  i first went into making biodegradable  face shields because  one of the issues that i'd always had  with my bio-based plastics was  they didn't have the longevity of  plastics because  of provide there was a mass increase of  single-use plastics being discarded  so for me it seemed like a great  opportunity to have a material which  didn't have a longevity of plastic that  could degrade  back into the earth the more  that we start understanding about  natural materialization and  understanding about the earth  it's really the best way that we're  actually going to start becoming  more sustainable

